# pbinfo — Competitive Programming

1000+ problems solved. Top 100 in my city.

## What It Is

[pbinfo.ro](https://www.pbinfo.ro) is Romania's largest competitive programming platform. It's where thousands of students grind algorithms, data structures, and problem-solving skills — from basic loops to advanced graph theory.

## The Grind

Over several years, I solved over 1000 problems spanning:

- **Data Structures**: Arrays, matrices, stacks, queues, heaps, hash maps, segment trees
- **Algorithms**: Sorting, searching, greedy, divide & conquer, backtracking, binary search
- **Dynamic Programming**: Knapsack, LIS, LCS, matrix chain, state DP
- **Graph Theory**: BFS, DFS, Dijkstra, Floyd-Warshall, topological sort, MST
- **Mathematics**: Number theory, combinatorics, modular arithmetic, prime sieves

## What I Learned

Competitive programming teaches you to think in edge cases. Your solution either passes all test cases in under a second, or it doesn't. There's no "mostly works." That mindset — obsessing over correctness and efficiency — carries into every other project I build.

Reaching top 100 in my city wasn't about being a genius. It was about consistency: showing up, failing, debugging, and trying again until the green "Accepted" finally appeared.

